    slug: "html-css-why-is-html-fundamentals-important-2",
    shortDescription: "Frequently asked HTML-CSS interview question about HTML fundamentals.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nIt matters because hTML structures web documents with elements and attributes. In practice, the example shows how that behavior is used: a product page might use headings, a navigation element, a form, and buttons so the browser has a meaningful document structure.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe question is looking for reasoning rather than another definition. Explain the problem the concept solves, then say what would make you choose a different approach.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. State the problem or need.\n2. Explain how HTML fundamentals addresses it: HTML structures web documents with elements and attributes. Browsers parse that markup into a DOM that scripts and styles can work with.\n3. Tie that benefit to the concrete situation: A product page might use headings, a navigation element, a form, and buttons so the browser has a meaningful document structure.\n4. State the condition that can make the approach a poor fit: HTML gives structure rather than visual design; good semantics can improve accessibility and maintainability.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nAnswer the “why” directly, then connect it to a real engineering constraint. I would give one concrete situation and close by saying what would make me choose another approach.\n\n**Example :**\nA product page might use headings, a navigation element, a form, and buttons so the browser has a meaningful document structure.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA web application may use HTML fundamentals when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a product page might use headings, a navigation element, a form, and buttons so the browser has a meaningful document structure. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating HTML fundamentals as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with HTML fundamentals.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nDo not repeat the definition as your whole answer. Explain the problem, the practical value, and the condition that would change your decision.",
