    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nWhen DevOps fundamentals misbehaves, start by reproducing the symptom and verifying the assumptions around the feature. Then inspect the inputs, state, dependencies, and evidence most relevant to DevOps fundamentals. DevOps combines development and operations practices to deliver and run software more reliably through automation, feedback, collaboration, and repeatable processes.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nTroubleshooting questions reveal whether you can narrow a problem using evidence instead of changing several things at once.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Reproduce the failure and capture the exact symptom.\n2. Check the part of the system that controls DevOps fundamentals: DevOps combines development and operations practices to deliver and run software more reliably through automation, feedback, collaboration, and repeatable processes.\n3. Use the concrete workflow as a comparison point: A team can automate tests, artifact creation, deployment, monitoring, and rollback instead of performing each step manually.\n4. Confirm the fix with a targeted regression check and watch for the trade-off: Automation reduces manual work but moves responsibility toward maintaining the pipeline and operational controls.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would reproduce the problem first and collect evidence before changing code. Then I would inspect the component or state most closely tied to the symptom, make one controlled change, and verify the result with a regression test or equivalent check.\n\n**Example :**\nA team can automate tests, artifact creation, deployment, monitoring, and rollback instead of performing each step manually.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA software delivery pipeline may use DevOps fundamentals when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a team can automate tests, artifact creation, deployment, monitoring, and rollback instead of performing each step manually. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating DevOps fundamentals as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with DevOps fundamentals.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nTalk through your investigation order. Interviewers learn more from your evidence-gathering and narrowing strategy than from hearing a long list of possible causes.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nWhen DevOps fundamentals misbehaves, start by reproducing the symptom and verifying the assumptions around the feature. Then inspect the inputs, state, dependencies, and evidence most relevant to DevOps fundamentals. DevOps combines development and operations practices to deliver and run software more reliably through automation, feedback, collaboration, and repeatable processes.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nTroubleshooting questions reveal whether you can narrow a problem using evidence instead of changing several things at once.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Reproduce the failure and capture the exact symptom.\n2. Check the part of the system that controls DevOps fundamentals: DevOps combines development and operations practices to deliver and run software more reliably through automation, feedback, collaboration, and repeatable processes.\n3. Use the concrete workflow as a comparison point: A team can automate tests, artifact creation, deployment, monitoring, and rollback instead of performing each step manually.\n4. Confirm the fix with a targeted regression check and watch for the trade-off: Automation reduces manual work but moves responsibility toward maintaining the pipeline and operational controls.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would reproduce the problem first and collect evidence before changing code. Then I would inspect the component or state most closely tied to the symptom, make one controlled change, and verify the result with a regression test or equivalent check.\n\n**Example :**\nA team can automate tests, artifact creation, deployment, monitoring, and rollback instead of performing each step manually.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA software delivery pipeline may use DevOps fundamentals when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a team can automate tests, artifact creation, deployment, monitoring, and rollback instead of performing each step manually. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating DevOps fundamentals as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with DevOps fundamentals.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nTalk through your investigation order. Interviewers learn more from your evidence-gathering and narrowing strategy than from hearing a long list of possible causes.",
