    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nIt matters because infrastructure as Code describes infrastructure declaratively or programmatically so it can be versioned, reviewed, and reproduced. In practice, the example shows how that behavior is used: a Terraform configuration can define a VPC, subnets, and load balancer rather than requiring manual console changes.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe question is looking for reasoning rather than another definition. Explain the problem the concept solves, then say what would make you choose a different approach.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. State the problem or need.\n2. Explain how IaC addresses it: Infrastructure as Code describes infrastructure declaratively or programmatically so it can be versioned, reviewed, and reproduced.\n3. Tie that benefit to the concrete situation: A Terraform configuration can define a VPC, subnets, and load balancer rather than requiring manual console changes.\n4. State the condition that can make the approach a poor fit: IaC improves repeatability but introduces state, dependency, and change-management concerns.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nAnswer the “why” directly, then connect it to a real engineering constraint. I would give one concrete situation and close by saying what would make me choose another approach.\n\n**Example :**\nA Terraform configuration can define a VPC, subnets, and load balancer rather than requiring manual console changes.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA software delivery pipeline may use IaC when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a Terraform configuration can define a VPC, subnets, and load balancer rather than requiring manual console changes. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating IaC as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with IaC.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nDo not repeat the definition as your whole answer. Explain the problem, the practical value, and the condition that would change your decision.",
