    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nGenerative AI fundamentals is useful when its benefits justify the costs or complexity it introduces. Generated output is probabilistic, so evaluation, grounding, and safety controls are important. The decision should be based on the actual requirement, not on a blanket rule.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis question tests engineering judgment. The interviewer wants to hear both sides and the constraint that determines the choice.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. State what Generative AI fundamentals gives you: Generative AI models learn patterns in data and generate outputs such as text, images, audio, or code from inputs. Modern language-model applications typically combine a model with prompts, tools, retrieval, and application logic.\n2. State what it costs or complicates: Generated output is probabilistic, so evaluation, grounding, and safety controls are important.\n3. Use this example to show where the trade-off appears: A support assistant can generate a draft response from the user question plus retrieved product documentation.\n4. Say when you would choose a simpler alternative.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would explain the benefit first, then the cost, and finally the condition that makes the trade-off worthwhile. I would avoid presenting one side as universally correct.\n\n**Example :**\nA support assistant can generate a draft response from the user question plus retrieved product documentation.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nAn ai-powered application may use Generative AI fundamentals when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a support assistant can generate a draft response from the user question plus retrieved product documentation. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Generative AI fundamentals as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Generative AI fundamentals.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nMake the trade-off concrete. Say what improves, what gets harder, and which constraint makes the decision reasonable.",
